# Breakdown staging (Kinsenas)

When a task finishes with a **breakdown file** (`.cursor/breakdowns/`) or an **implementation summary** (changelog bullets at end of reply), **stage all files for that task** so the user can commit manually. Multiple agents or tasks may modify the repo at once — staging must be **scoped to this task only**.

Related: [plan-implementation.mdc](./plan-implementation.mdc).

## When to stage

| Trigger | Stage? |
| ------- | ------ |
| Full workflow — breakdown + implementation summary | **Yes** |
| Lightweight workflow — implementation summary only (no breakdown) | **Yes**, if app/docs/rules files changed |
| Question-only / review-only — no code or breakdown | No |

Run staging **before** the final reply, after tests and formatting are done.

## What to stage

Stage every path that belongs to **this task**:

1. Breakdown file (`.cursor/breakdowns/YYYYMMDD-HHMM-<task-slug>-breakdown.md`)
2. Plan file when this task created or updated one (`.cursor/plans/…`)
3. Every path under **Files touched** in the breakdown (or the equivalent list you would put there)
4. Any new/edited files from this session that support the same feature but were easy to miss (generated routes, lockfiles when deps changed, etc.)

**Do not** stage files you did not touch for this task, even if they appear in `git status`.

## Concurrent tasks — strict boundaries

- **Never** `git add .`, `git add -A`, or `git add -u` without explicit paths.
- **Never** `git reset`, `git restore --staged`, or otherwise unstage files — other tasks may already have staged theirs.
- **Never** `git commit` or `git push` unless the user explicitly asks ([plan-implementation.mdc](./plan-implementation.mdc) §5).
- If a file was edited for multiple tasks and you cannot split it, **do not stage it**; note in the reply that it needs a manual decision.

## How to stage

Use explicit paths (one `git add` with multiple paths is fine):

```bash
git add .cursor/breakdowns/20260817-0438-example-breakdown.md app/Http/Controllers/ExampleController.php resources/js/pages/example.tsx
```

On Windows/PowerShell, quote paths that contain spaces or brackets.

## Report in the final reply

After staging, include a short **Staged for commit** block:

```markdown
## Staged for commit

- `.cursor/breakdowns/…-breakdown.md`
- `app/…`
- `resources/js/…`

**Not staged** (other work / shared edits): `path/if/any`
```

If nothing was staged (no file changes), say so — do not run `git add` unnecessarily.
